{
  "info": {
    "name": "Payment System - Call Every Controller Directly",
    "description": "Hits each service's controller directly - not just through the orchestrated flow - so you can see what each hop in the authorization chain actually does on its own. Folder 2 is the interesting one: it calls Merchant, Acquirer, Network, and Issuer's controllers one at a time, the same way transaction-service does internally. Folder 3 shows the same thing happening automatically when you call the real entry points.\n\nStart the services first (service-registry, merchant-service, acquirer-service, network-service, issuer-service, transaction-service, pos-terminal-service - see GETTING-STARTED.md or run ./start-all.sh), then run Folder 1 top to bottom once to populate merchantId/cardNumber/cvv, then explore Folders 2-4 in any order.",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
  },
  "variable": [
    { "key": "merchantUrl", "value": "http://localhost:8081" },
    { "key": "acquirerUrl", "value": "http://localhost:8082" },
    { "key": "issuerUrl", "value": "http://localhost:8083" },
    { "key": "networkUrl", "value": "http://localhost:8084" },
    { "key": "transactionUrl", "value": "http://localhost:8085" },
    { "key": "posUrl", "value": "http://localhost:8091" },
    { "key": "merchantId", "value": "" },
    { "key": "cardId", "value": "" },
    { "key": "cardNumber", "value": "" },
    { "key": "cvv", "value": "" },
    { "key": "transactionId", "value": "" }
  ],
  "item": [
    {
      "name": "1. Setup (run these three first)",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "Create Merchant",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "exec": [
                  "const body = pm.response.json();",
                  "pm.collectionVariables.set('merchantId', body.id);",
                  "pm.test('merchant created', () => pm.response.code === 201);",
                  "pm.test('status is PENDING_VERIFICATION', () => body.status === 'PENDING_VERIFICATION');"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [{ "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" }],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"businessName\": \"Coffee Shop\",\n  \"email\": \"shop-{{$randomInt}}@coffee.com\",\n  \"phone\": \"+12025550123\",\n  \"address\": \"123 Main Street\",\n  \"taxId\": \"12-3456789-{{$randomInt}}\",\n  \"merchantCategoryCode\": \"5814\",\n  \"dailyLimit\": 10000,\n  \"monthlyLimit\": 300000\n}"
            },
            "url": { "raw": "{{merchantUrl}}/api/merchants", "host": ["{{merchantUrl}}"], "path": ["api", "merchants"] },
            "description": "MerchantController.createMerchant(). New merchants start PENDING_VERIFICATION - nothing can transact against them until activated below."
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "Activate Merchant",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "exec": [
                  "const body = pm.response.json();",
                  "pm.test('status is ACTIVE', () => body.status === 'ACTIVE');"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "PUT",
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{merchantUrl}}/api/merchants/{{merchantId}}/status?status=ACTIVE",
              "host": ["{{merchantUrl}}"], "path": ["api", "merchants", "{{merchantId}}", "status"],
              "query": [{ "key": "status", "value": "ACTIVE" }]
            },
            "description": "MerchantController.updateStatus(). Every merchant-limit check downstream fails until this runs."
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "Issue Card",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "exec": [
                  "const body = pm.response.json();",
                  "pm.collectionVariables.set('cardId', body.id);",
                  "pm.collectionVariables.set('cardNumber', body.cardNumber);",
                  "pm.collectionVariables.set('cvv', body.cvv);",
                  "pm.test('card issued', () => pm.response.code === 201);",
                  "pm.test('full PAN/CVV returned at issuance', () => body.cardNumber && body.cardNumber.length === 16 && body.cvv);"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [{ "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" }],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"cardholderName\": \"John Doe\",\n  \"cardType\": \"CREDIT\",\n  \"network\": \"VISA\",\n  \"creditLimit\": 5000\n}"
            },
            "url": { "raw": "{{issuerUrl}}/api/cards", "host": ["{{issuerUrl}}"], "path": ["api", "cards"] },
            "description": "IssuerController.issueCard(). This is the ONLY endpoint that ever returns the full, unmasked card number and CVV - every other card endpoint masks them. That's why cardNumber/cvv get captured here into collection variables for the rest of the requests to use."
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "2. Call Each Controller Directly (understand one hop at a time)",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "Merchant - Validate For Transaction",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{merchantUrl}}/api/merchants/{{merchantId}}/validate?amount=25.99",
              "host": ["{{merchantUrl}}"], "path": ["api", "merchants", "{{merchantId}}", "validate"],
              "query": [{ "key": "amount", "value": "25.99" }]
            },
            "description": "MerchantController.validateForTransaction(). Checks the merchant is ACTIVE and that this amount wouldn't blow past its daily/monthly limit. This is the FIRST thing transaction-service calls before anything else - a merchant that fails this never even reaches the acquirer."
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "Acquirer - Process Acquiring (fraud/velocity check)",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [{ "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" }],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"merchantId\": \"{{merchantId}}\",\n  \"cardNumber\": \"{{cardNumber}}\",\n  \"amount\": 25.99,\n  \"terminalId\": \"TERM0001\"\n}"
            },
            "url": { "raw": "{{acquirerUrl}}/api/acquirers/process", "host": ["{{acquirerUrl}}"], "path": ["api", "acquirers", "process"] },
            "description": "AcquirerController.processAcquiring() - the merchant's bank running fraud/velocity screening. Response includes fraudScore so you can see the number behind the approve/decline call. Note: with today's scoring formula the max reachable score is 49 against an 80-point decline threshold, so this always approves - worth noticing while you explore."
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "Network - Route Transaction",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [{ "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" }],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"cardNumber\": \"{{cardNumber}}\",\n  \"amount\": 25.99\n}"
            },
            "url": { "raw": "{{networkUrl}}/api/network/route", "host": ["{{networkUrl}}"], "path": ["api", "network", "route"] },
            "description": "NetworkController.routeTransaction() - identifies the card network from its first digit (BIN) and calculates the network's interchange fee. Try changing cardNumber's first digit (4=VISA, 5=MASTERCARD, 3=AMEX, anything else=LOCAL) and re-running to see the fee change."
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "Network - Identify Card Network (GET)",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{networkUrl}}/api/network/identify/{{cardNumber}}",
              "host": ["{{networkUrl}}"], "path": ["api", "network", "identify", "{{cardNumber}}"]
            },
            "description": "NetworkController.identifyNetwork() - just the BIN lookup, no fee calculation."
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "Issuer - Authorize (basic, no PIN/MAC/EMV)",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [{ "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" }],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"cardNumber\": \"{{cardNumber}}\",\n  \"cvv\": \"{{cvv}}\",\n  \"amount\": 25.99,\n  \"currency\": \"USD\",\n  \"merchantId\": \"{{merchantId}}\"\n}"
            },
            "url": { "raw": "{{issuerUrl}}/api/cards/authorize", "host": ["{{issuerUrl}}"], "path": ["api", "cards", "authorize"] },
            "description": "IssuerController.authorize() - the cardholder's own bank making the final call: card active? not blocked? CVV correct? enough available balance? This is the actual last-mile decision every other hop in the chain leads up to. Try a wrong CVV or an amount over 5000 (the card's credit limit) to see it decline."
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "Issuer - Block Card",
          "request": {
            "method": "PUT",
            "url": { "raw": "{{issuerUrl}}/api/cards/{{cardId}}/block", "host": ["{{issuerUrl}}"], "path": ["api", "cards", "{{cardId}}", "block"] },
            "description": "Block the card, then re-run 'Issuer - Authorize' above to see it decline with 'Card is blocked'."
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "Issuer - Unblock Card",
          "request": {
            "method": "PUT",
            "url": { "raw": "{{issuerUrl}}/api/cards/{{cardId}}/unblock", "host": ["{{issuerUrl}}"], "path": ["api", "cards", "{{cardId}}", "unblock"] },
            "description": "Undo the block above."
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "3. Full Orchestrated Flow (transaction-service calls all four above for you)",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "Transaction - Authorize (approved example)",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "exec": [
                  "const body = pm.response.json();",
                  "pm.collectionVariables.set('transactionId', body.id);",
                  "pm.test('AUTHORIZED', () => body.status === 'AUTHORIZED');"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [{ "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" }],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"merchantId\": \"{{merchantId}}\",\n  \"cardNumber\": \"{{cardNumber}}\",\n  \"cvv\": \"{{cvv}}\",\n  \"terminalId\": \"TERM0001\",\n  \"type\": \"PURCHASE\",\n  \"amount\": 25.99,\n  \"currency\": \"USD\"\n}"
            },
            "url": { "raw": "{{transactionUrl}}/api/transactions/authorize", "host": ["{{transactionUrl}}"], "path": ["api", "transactions", "authorize"] },
            "description": "TransactionController.authorize() - the real orchestrated entry point. Internally this calls the exact same four controllers from Folder 2, in order: Merchant -> Acquirer -> Network -> Issuer, stopping at whichever one says no. Watch each service's own console/log while this runs to see all four fire within milliseconds of each other."
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "Transaction - Authorize (declined: exceeds daily limit)",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [{ "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" }],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"merchantId\": \"{{merchantId}}\",\n  \"cardNumber\": \"{{cardNumber}}\",\n  \"cvv\": \"{{cvv}}\",\n  \"terminalId\": \"TERM0001\",\n  \"type\": \"PURCHASE\",\n  \"amount\": 9999.00,\n  \"currency\": \"USD\"\n}"
            },
            "url": { "raw": "{{transactionUrl}}/api/transactions/authorize", "host": ["{{transactionUrl}}"], "path": ["api", "transactions", "authorize"] },
            "description": "Same endpoint, an amount that pushes the merchant over its $10,000 daily limit. Returns 200 OK with status: DECLINED and responseCode 03 - declines are a normal business outcome here, not an HTTP error (see TESTING.md for why that matters for Feign callers like the POS terminal)."
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "Transaction - Get By Id",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "url": { "raw": "{{transactionUrl}}/api/transactions/{{transactionId}}", "host": ["{{transactionUrl}}"], "path": ["api", "transactions", "{{transactionId}}"] },
            "description": "Fetch the persisted record back independently of the authorize response - proves it actually landed in the database, with the acquirerId/networkId/issuerId trail populated."
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "Transaction - Get All For Merchant",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "url": { "raw": "{{transactionUrl}}/api/transactions/merchant/{{merchantId}}", "host": ["{{transactionUrl}}"], "path": ["api", "transactions", "merchant", "{{merchantId}}"] }
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "Transaction - Refund",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "url": { "raw": "{{transactionUrl}}/api/transactions/{{transactionId}}/refund", "host": ["{{transactionUrl}}"], "path": ["api", "transactions", "{{transactionId}}", "refund"] },
            "description": "Only works on an AUTHORIZED/CAPTURED/SETTLED transaction - run the approved request above first. Returns 409 if the transaction isn't in a refundable state."
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "4. POS Terminal (the real card-present simulation)",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "POS - Chip + PIN Purchase (approved)",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [{ "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" }],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"terminalId\": \"TERM0001\",\n  \"merchantId\": \"{{merchantId}}\",\n  \"merchantName\": \"Coffee Shop\",\n  \"amount\": 2599,\n  \"cardReadMethod\": \"CHIP\",\n  \"requirePIN\": true,\n  \"pin\": \"1234\",\n  \"cardNumber\": \"{{cardNumber}}\",\n  \"expiryDate\": \"2812\",\n  \"cvv\": \"{{cvv}}\"\n}"
            },
            "url": { "raw": "{{posUrl}}/api/pos/transaction", "host": ["{{posUrl}}"], "path": ["api", "pos", "transaction"] },
            "description": "POSController.processTransaction() - the terminal itself: reads the card, formats+encrypts a PIN block, generates an EMV cryptogram, builds an ISO 8583 message, signs it with a MAC, THEN calls Transaction - Authorize above over real HTTP (not simulated). amount is in CENTS here, unlike every other endpoint in this collection which uses dollars - that's a real inconsistency between this simulated terminal and the rest of the system, worth noticing. The response includes a printable receipt string."
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "POS - Chip + PIN Purchase (declined: exceeds daily limit)",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [{ "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" }],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"terminalId\": \"TERM0001\",\n  \"merchantId\": \"{{merchantId}}\",\n  \"merchantName\": \"Coffee Shop\",\n  \"amount\": 999900,\n  \"cardReadMethod\": \"CHIP\",\n  \"requirePIN\": true,\n  \"pin\": \"1234\",\n  \"cardNumber\": \"{{cardNumber}}\",\n  \"expiryDate\": \"2812\",\n  \"cvv\": \"{{cvv}}\"\n}"
            },
            "url": { "raw": "{{posUrl}}/api/pos/transaction", "host": ["{{posUrl}}"], "path": ["api", "pos", "transaction"] },
            "description": "$9,999.00 in cents. The receipt field in the response will show the SPECIFIC decline reason from transaction-service (\"Daily limit exceeded\"), not a generic code description."
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "POS - Magnetic Stripe, No PIN",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [{ "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" }],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"terminalId\": \"TERM0001\",\n  \"merchantId\": \"{{merchantId}}\",\n  \"merchantName\": \"Coffee Shop\",\n  \"amount\": 1500,\n  \"cardReadMethod\": \"MAGNETIC_STRIPE\",\n  \"requirePIN\": false,\n  \"cardNumber\": \"{{cardNumber}}\",\n  \"expiryDate\": \"2812\",\n  \"cvv\": \"{{cvv}}\"\n}"
            },
            "url": { "raw": "{{posUrl}}/api/pos/transaction", "host": ["{{posUrl}}"], "path": ["api", "pos", "transaction"] },
            "description": "Compare the response's emvVerified/pinVerified fields against the CHIP+PIN request above - EMV only runs for CHIP reads."
          }
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}
